A stop takes a waiting thread off its wait but leaves its pc past the call it waited in,
so a resume goes on as if the wait had returned, with registers the call never wrote:
a waiter stands at the call it waited in.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a stop left a waiting thread elsewhere than at the call it waited in
Witness: fuzz cores-waiter-stopped

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -454,7 +454,6 @@ static bool thread_stop(struct thread *t)
 {
     if (t->state == THREAD_WAITING) {
         unwait(t);
-        t->frame.pc -= CALL_SIZE;
     }
     t->state = THREAD_STOPPED;
     return core_thread_stopped(t);
